                <!-- Bug 869eg53ep: "Meet The Team" button reported as duplicated while the
                     page is open in the website builder's edit mode. This <a> mixes a
                     t-field (the editable label) with a plain decorative sibling (the arrow
                     glyph) inside the same editable root — the same shape of problem already
                     solved elsewhere in this codebase (see the t-ignore usage on
                     .atl-video-select-overlay in atlasco_about_page.xml / atlasco_careers_page.xml)
                     where a non-field sibling sitting next to editable content gets swept up
                     by the editor's generic raw-HTML/contenteditable normalization and can be
                     re-inserted alongside the field, reading as a duplicated block. Marking the
                     arrow t-ignore keeps it out of the editable/normalizable area entirely so
                     only the single t-field span is ever treated as editable content; no visual
                     or behavioral change for normal visitors. -->
                <a href="/careers" class="cine-btn cine-btn--green" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:#1f9a51;color:#fff;border:none;border-radius:12px;padding:16px 30px;font-family:inherit;font-size:16px;font-weight:700;cursor:pointer;box-shadow:0 14px 30px rgba(31,154,81,.34);"><span t-field="content.home_careers_btn"/> <span t-ignore="1" contenteditable="false" style="font-size:19px;">&#8594;</span></a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
